{
  "//": "V17.6 OFB-1 — outcome feedback on scores (owner « V176 : DÉBLOCAGE FINAL » item 3). Per-criterion ATTRIBUTION rule OFB-CAL-2 (varying selection-time values AND |Spearman ρ| ≥ RHO_MIN with the realized utility, n ≥ MIN_N) from measured + inspected closure grades only; applied to the strategic register ONLY while the committed activation record binds these adjustments. Recompute: npx tsx runtime/bin/odg-v176-outcome-feedback.ts --check",
  "schema": "ODG_V176_OUTCOME_FEEDBACK/1",
  "feedbackVersion": "OFB-1",
  "ownerDirective": {
    "record": "docs/odg/V176_OWNER_DIRECTIVE_DEBLOCAGE_FINAL.json",
    "recordPresentOnThisTree": true,
    "item": 3,
    "quote": "Rétroaction des résultats sur les scores : j'autorise désormais son développement et son activation contrôlée. Utiliser uniquement des résultats mesurés et attribuables, conserver l'historique des scores, rendre les changements traçables et réversibles. Ne jamais transformer une hypothèse ou une simulation en preuve réelle."
  },
  "rules": {
    "OFB-ADM-1": "an outcome is ADMITTED iff (a) the register item is CLOSE-1 closed with grade PASS|PARTIAL|FAIL (CLOSED_NOT_MEASURED ⇒ refused); (b) its criteria-validation record has schema odg-criteria-validation/1, names the item, grades it with the SAME grade, and is bound to the closure's contract sha256 AND experiment sha256; (c) the record carries an independent inspection ACCEPT (experimentInspection.verdict ACCEPT, distinct opaque inspectorSessionId / authorSessionId); (d) neither the validation nor the experiment record is a PROBE / simulation / fixture / hypothesis / synthetic / mock / dry-run / prediction (identity fields path, schema, label, kind, basis; or a true simulated/probe/fixture/hypothesis flag); (e) a selection-time prediction is attributable (register criteria read from committed git history, with a source pointer). Anything else is REFUSED with its reason and never used",
    "OFB-PRED-1": "the prediction of an admitted item is the register's criteria AT SELECTION TIME — odg-v175-outcome-learning gatherSelection over the committed history of V164_STRATEGIC_REGISTER.json up to the experiment's run head (the same rule the V17.5 outcome-learning record uses); favourability = value (HIGHER_IS_BETTER) or 1 − value (LOWER_IS_BETTER), only for MEASURED criteria",
    "OFB-CAL-2": "per criterion c: obs = admitted items where c was MEASURED at selection time, x = favourability (value, or 1 − value when LOWER_IS_BETTER), y = realized utility PASS=1 / PARTIAL=0.5 / FAIL=0 (odg-outcome-learning.GRADE_UTILITY). Adjusted ONLY IF (i) n ≥ 5, (ii) x is not constant (non-zero variance), (iii) ρ = odg-rank-correlation.spearman(x, y) is defined (y not constant) and (iv) |ρ| ≥ 0.5; then multiplier = round4(1 + 0.2·ρ) ∈ [0.8, 1.2] (ρ > 0: higher predicted favourability preceded better grades ⇒ the criterion's contributions are raised; ρ < 0 ⇒ lowered). Otherwise multiplier 1, status NOT_ATTRIBUTABLE with the failing condition. Supersedes OFB-CAL-1 (base-rate level shift = mean favourability − mean utility), REJECTED at inspection because it adjusted criteria whose values carry no information about the grade. ρ over n ≈ 5 is an ORDER association on these items, not causation and not significance",
    "OFB-APPLY-1": "when ACTIVE, mission-priority-selector.scoreExplained multiplies each MEASURED criterion contribution by its multiplier (absent ⇒ 1); NOT_MEASURED criteria still contribute 0 and their full weight to uncertainty (never imputed); every breakdown row keeps baseContribution + multiplier and every ranked row keeps baseEvidenceScore + scoreDelta; thresholds, weights, criteria values, statuses, eligibility and the secondary rules are unchanged",
    "OFB-ACT-1": "OFF by default. ACTIVE iff the committed activation record (docs/odg/V176_OUTCOME_FEEDBACK_ACTIVATION.json) has schema odg-outcome-feedback-activation/1, active === true, feedbackVersion OFB-1, the owner quote VERBATIM, ownerRecord docs/odg/V176_OWNER_DIRECTIVE_DEBLOCAGE_FINAL.json (when that file is present on the tree it must contain the quote, else OFF), and adjustmentsSha256 equal to sha256(canon(adjustments)) of the layer being applied; any other state ⇒ OFF with its reason",
    "OFB-RB-1": "rollback = set active:false in the activation record (and append a DEACTIVATE history entry): the selector then receives no multipliers and the strategic register is byte-identical to the base register; a new set of adjustments (e.g. a new graded item) is NEVER applied until a new activation record binds its sha",
    "OFB-HIST-1": "docs/odg/evidence/V176_OUTCOME_FEEDBACK_HISTORY.jsonl is append-only JSON lines, hash-chained (prevSha256 = sha256 of the previous line); every ACTIVATE / DEACTIVATE appends the adjustments sha, the multipliers, the base and adjusted score of every ranked item and the strategic + actionable decisions before/after; earlier lines are never rewritten"
  },
